"""Human-readable reporting of frozen results; no inference or new hypothesis tests."""
import csv,json
from core import HERE
r=json.loads((HERE/'RESULTS.json').read_text());p=r['primary'];s=r['secondary'];models=['qwen7b','llama3b']
def number(x):return 'undefined' if x is None else f'{x:.4f}'
lines=['# Prospective competence-selection confirmation','', '## Decision','', ('**NARROW: the prespecified construction-dependent screen effect replicated in this panel. No new linguistic mechanism is established.**' if p['supported'] else '**NO-GO for the prespecified construction-dependent screen confirmation. The complete fixed panel is retained.**'),'', 'One frozen experiment:24 fresh lexical families ×8 role/voice/question prompts ×2 existing local quantized checkpoints. No answer-based collection exclusions, threshold refits, site changes, retries or follow-up model experiments. The pre-output source freeze is [a376dcf](https://github.com/Joel-Vazquez-Lopez/relational-transfer/commit/a376dcf46e4d2bc26fe592ace1fe674683c5dcf9). All15 frozen publication files were verified before the first new forward.','', '## Complete native and fixed-threshold results','', 'A unit is four role×question answers for one family and one voice. A family contains two units. These are AI-authored synthetic sentences, not natural documents. Native means vocabulary-wide first-token argmax, not full generated responses. The fixed external classifier is a different decision rule.','', '|Checkpoint|Construction|Native answers /96|Fixed threshold /96|Native complete units /24|Fixed-threshold complete units /24|Separable units /24|','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for t in r['totals']:lines.append(f"|{t['model']}|{t['voice']}|{t['native_correct']}|{t['calibrated_correct']}|{t['native_complete']}|{t['calibrated_complete']}|{t['separable']}|")
lines+=['','## Sole confirmatory test','',f"For each Qwen lexical family, d = (calibrated−native complete-active indicator) − (calibrated−native complete-passive indicator). Positive:{p['positive']}; negative:{p['negative']}; tied:{p['ties']}. Mean d:{p['mean_d']:.4f}. Prespecified one-sided exact family sign test **p={p['one_sided_p']:.8g}**, alpha .05; criterion {'passed' if p['supported'] else 'failed'}.",'', 'This p value is conditional on independent/exchangeable family signs under the null. The24 families are an authored fixed list with shared templates, not a randomized linguistic population. It is not a probability that the hypothesis is true, proof of generalization, or a novelty test. No separate Llama, answer-level, layer-level or secondary p values were calculated.','', '### Every family-level primary outcome','', '|Family|Qwen d|Llama d (descriptive)|Qwen native whole-family /1|Qwen calibrated whole-family /1|Llama native whole-family /1|Llama calibrated whole-family /1|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for f in r['families']:
 q,l=[f['models'][m] for m in models];lines.append(f"|{f['family']}|{q['d']}|{l['d']}|{int(q['native_whole_family'])}|{int(q['calibrated_whole_family'])}|{int(l['native_whole_family'])}|{int(l['calibrated_whole_family'])}|")
lines+=['','## Fixed causal comparison: does the earlier gap illustration reproduce?','', 'The assay is the old source-isolated period mask at cut14. D is the four-answer role×question contrast of the Yes−No alias score. Retention is D_mask/D_native, undefined for |D_native|<.5. The mask and score are identical across gates: only eligible rows change. Selected means estimate different conditional samples, not changes in the model.','', '|Gate|Support policy|Qwen mean retention (valid n)|Llama mean retention (valid n)|Llama−Qwen|','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in r['profiles']:
 if x['mode']!='frozen' or x['gate'] not in ['all','native_complete','calibrated_complete']:continue
 q,l=[x['models'][m] for m in models];lines.append(f"|{x['gate']}|{x['policy']}|{number(q['mean_retention'])} ({q['n_ratio']})|{number(l['mean_retention'])} ({l['n_ratio']})|{number(x['gap'])}|")
lines+=['',f"Own-selected gap shift (native-gated minus all): **{number(s['delta_gap'])}**. The frozen descriptive replication criterion was a positive shift ≥.10: **{'met' if s['descriptive_replication'] else 'not met'}**. Common native-gate gap shift:{number(s['common_delta_gap'])}; {'same positive direction' if s['matched_support_direction'] else 'no same-direction confirmation on this support'}. These are descriptive comparisons with no secondary significance test.",'', 'The earlier post hoc example was .2831→.5320. A successful primary selection test does not make that causal-gap illustration a replicated finding; the secondary criterion is judged separately. Full raw D means, medians, denominator exclusions, negative native D, common selections, whole-family gates and closed/irrelevant masks are all retained in RESULTS.json. Inspect `ratio_units` separately from selected units: a common gate is not automatically common valid-denominator support.','', '## Why a native failure is not automatically a relational deficit','']
for m in models:
 us=[u for u in r['units'] if u['model']==m];removed=[u for u in us if not u['native_complete']];inside=[u for u in removed if u['threshold_inside']];separate=[u for u in removed if u['separable'] and not u['threshold_inside']];overlap=[u for u in removed if not u['separable']]
 lines.append(f"- **{m}:**{len(removed)}/48 native-incomplete units;{len(inside)} have a separating interval containing the old fixed threshold;{len(separate)} are separated but that threshold misses;{len(overlap)} have overlapping/tied Yes/No ranges. Baseline off-label argmax answers:{sum(u['off_label'] for u in us)}. Every unit's offset, R/Q terms, D and interval is in UNIT_LEDGER.csv and RESULTS.json.")
lines+=['', 'A separating interval shows only that these four final scores can be classified by a scalar boundary. It does not show native correctness, an internal calibrated posterior, or a specific semantic mechanism. The question and correct answer already determine role orientation on this binary support; syntax-aware copying and output preparation remain competing accounts.','', '## Numerical and preservation audit','',f"- **{r['n_forwards']}/1562** actual forwards,781 per checkpoint, including native-wrapper/repeat, sham and cut0-disconnection controls.",f"- **{sum(r['production_controls'].values())} production numerical checks** passed; **{r['n_independent_checks']} independent replay checks** passed. No numerical gate was loosened and no frozen source changed.",'- Every attempt was journaled before dispatch; every full output vector was saved losslessly before scoring. Raw outputs include all wrong, off-label, surprising and intervention-produced answers. Native residual traces have all29 stages at period and answer; intervention traces have five saved anchors plus full-trace hashes.','- The archive manifest/shards reconstruct every1562 original NPZ files with per-member SHA256 verification. Full token-prefix arrays were stored as hashes, not values. No KV, attention or MLP writes were captured here.','- No paid calls, downloads, model training or extra adaptive panel. Existing branches/previous failed gates are preserved. The synthetic1562-call controller rehearsals and small algebra tests are not counted as empirical model forwards.','', '## Relation to prior work and the original research objective','', 'This supplies a measurement audit for the Linguistic Development Observatory: define the target population and report construction-stratified evidence before interpreting a cross-model map built from correctness-filtered examples. It does not reconstruct how meaning develops inside a Transformer. One fixed cut cannot establish the temporal order of all functions.','', '[Jenner et al.(2024)](https://papers.nips.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/file/37d9f19150fce07bced2a81fc87d47a6-Paper-Conference.pdf) already report a structural shift in a filtered chess interpretability dataset; the general selection concern is not new. [Zhao et al.(2021)](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/zhao21c.html) already studies external calibration, and [Zhang & Nanda(2024)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.16042) establishes assay/metric sensitivity. [Dai et al.(2024)](https://aclanthology.org/2024.emnlp-main.967/) provides causal binding-subspace results that our present binary assay does not identify or replace. See LITERATURE_SCOPE.md for the precise narrower comparison.','', 'No universal mechanism, family-wide difference, novel calibration method or publishable-paper result is claimed. Active/passive alternation bundles tokens, length and position; AI argument labels are not uniformly strict Agent/Patient thematic roles. See LIMITATIONS.md and ANNOTATION_LIMITATIONS.md. The exact selection decomposition is a supplementary descriptive calculation, not another confirmatory test or causal mediation identification.','', '## Reproducible artifacts','', '- PROTOCOL.md, LOCK.json, FREEZE_RECEIPT.json: frozen predictions/inputs/sources and pre-inference GitHub receipt.','- SOURCE_MANIFEST.json, TOKENIZER_AUDIT.json: all24 lexical families, annotation uncertainties and freshness scope.','- ANSWER_LEDGER.csv, UNEXPECTED_ANSWERS.json, per-model RAW.jsonl and BUDGET.jsonl: every original answer and attempt.','- UNIT_LEDGER.csv, FAMILY_LEDGER.csv, RESULTS.json: individual scores remain separate from complete units and families.','- INDEPENDENT_AUDIT.json, per-model CONTROLS.json, DECISION.json: numerical and score-replay checks.','- CONFIRMATION.png/svg/pdf: descriptive figure; plot.py reproduces it.','- SELECTION_DECOMPOSITION.json: all fixed masks/gates, with construction-mixture and within-construction selection terms.','- PAYLOAD_ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.json and PAYLOADS.partNNN: all original full-output/trace NPZ payloads, losslessly reconstructable.','', '**Collection is complete. No additional inference follows this report.**','']
(HERE/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
fields=['model','family','voice','native_correct','calibrated_correct','native_complete','calibrated_complete','zero_threshold_correct','off_label','D_native','offset','role_term','question_term','separable','threshold_inside','all_ordinal_positive']+[f'{mode}_{key}' for mode in ['frozen','closed','irrelevant'] for key in ['D','retention','native_correct','calibrated_correct']]+['interval_low','interval_high']
with (HERE/'UNIT_LEDGER.csv').open('w') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields,extrasaction='ignore');w.writeheader()
 for u in r['units']:w.writerow({**u,'interval_low':u['interval'][0],'interval_high':u['interval'][1],**{f'{mode}_{k}':v for mode,x in u['interventions'].items() for k,v in x.items()}})
with (HERE/'FAMILY_LEDGER.csv').open('w') as f:
 fields=['family']+[m+'_'+k for m in models for k in ['d','native_whole_family','calibrated_whole_family']];w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);w.writeheader()
 for u in r['families']:w.writerow(dict(family=u['family'],**{m+'_'+k:v for m,x in u['models'].items() for k,v in x.items()}))
print('REPORT and separate unit/family ledgers written')
